awsuit is expected to be filed  this morning in Miami it will show  examples of other cruise lines that the  family attorney argues have safety  screens or windows that cannot be opened  at all the family attorney will also  argue in the suit that the cruise line  should have known window guidelines as  newer boats owned by Royal Caribbean  either have windows that don't open or  employ safety devices  like window screens or guards the suit  will also claim the large gap between  the handrail and the window made it hard  for anello to distinguish the open  window from glass he told us why that  may have happened I am color blind so  that's been me that's something that you  are colorblind colorblind Eve I don't  know I just never saw it I've been told  that that's a reason that it might have  happened and there was a note from a  doctor that diagnosed him with being  colorblind we saw that note in the  lawsuit the family is gonna ask to be  compensated for pain and mental  suffering now you should know we have  tried for weeks to get Royal Caribbean  to tell us their side of the story to  correct any misinformation and they have  not  they've only said that this was a tragic  incident they've offered condolences and  just this morning a very short time ago  they told us that they haven't even seen  the lawsuit so they would have no  further comment grandfather Anthony is  too important Porto Rico next week he is  charged with negligent homicide that  story in New Zealand in the story now  with the family Royal Caribbean has a  lot going on but I will never be  convinced that that grandfather should  be charged it just seems to be  prolonging the entire tragedy everybody  agrees that it's a tragic accident  alright David thank you
 

